{"baseRefName":"main","body":"LUBM generation now runs through an original first-party Rust generator instead of Java/JRE, UBA archives and filename repair. Its versioned native profile follows the published schema and cardinality constraints, emits deterministic N-Triples, and verifies actual generated/converted graphs and query answers through independent native oracles. It does not reproduce UBA's random sequence or historical answer pins.\n\nThe production Make lane retains verified ontology/query acquisition, all fourteen query/regime transformations, full/file/slice status laws and failure-certificate revocation. A caller-visible finite join-step budget applies consistently to entailment probes and measured queries. Custom schema/base configuration is projected through the actual RDF model and remains bound to the recorded inputs.\n\nValidation already completed: native CLI determinism and independently parsed graph constraints; four actual default/custom cold/warm Make runs with all fourteen queries OK/full; exact artifact parity; six real process/result failures; early admission, pinned-cache corruption/restoration and retained-run tamper controls; 106 current affected tests and offline acquisition checks. Default native Q1/Q14 sets contain 2/6141 results; the two-university index2 configuration has legitimate Q1=0 and Q14=14294. Timings are report-only.\n\nThe single full local `make check` passed, including warning-denied workspace/consumer checks, all hygiene/generated gates, native tests/doctests, the kernel ring fence and every required release WASM build. Independent completion review passed every current implementation/runtime criterion. Normal source commits and hooks passed; mandatory hosted CI/review and ghprsq integration remain pending.\n\nComparisons must use the same native profile, generated bytes, queries and regimes. These results do not establish UBA byte or answer equivalence, or a performance win over another engine.\n\nCloses #475\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added native LUBM university corpus generation with configurable size, seed, and ontology settings, plus receipts that record generated files and their integrity.\n  * The LUBM benchmark now checks generated data and query answers against RDF-derived results, and supports a configurable join-step limit.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated benchmark guidance to describe the native generator, pinned external ontology and query inputs, and the new profile and validation process.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","headRefName":"paudley/475-benchmarks-replace-the-java-lubm","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":503,"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37766448989/job/113275175995","name":"workspace","startedAt":"2026-10-08T10:53:31Z","status":"IN_PROGRESS","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37766448945/job/113275174289","name":"Build The PurRDF Book","startedAt":"2026-10-08T10:53:30Z","status":"IN_PROGRESS","workflowName":"Docs"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-08T10:54:17Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37766446745/job/113275172480","name":"Analyze (actions)","startedAt":"2026-10-08T10:53:30Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CodeQL"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-08T10:54:21Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/actions/runs/37766446745/job/113275172101","name":"Analyze (c-cpp)","startedAt":"2026-10-08T10:53:30Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CodeQL"},{"__typename":"Ch